WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.480
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am&nbsp;
going to explain a comedy film called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.960
“The Bandit Hound”. Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.760
Bandit is an Australian Shepherd&nbsp;
trained to be a thief by his masters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:25.440
Manny and Willy. In the opening scene, he&nbsp;
walks into a bank with a bag and a note&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.160
attached to it. The guard doesn’t care to&nbsp;
check the little dog and lets it through.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:35.040
The cashier reads the note that says&nbsp;
the dog is attached to an explosive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.760
which will go off if they do not fill&nbsp;
his backpack with hundred dollar bills.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:45.520
She quickly does as told, after which Bandit&nbsp;
runs away. Outside, his masters are waiting for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:51.120
him in a car. They check his bag and throw out a&nbsp;
tracking device used as a trap. It turns out that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:57.680
the explosive was fake, used as a way to scare the&nbsp;
cashier. While Manny praises Bandit for his work,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:03.360
Willy isn’t fond of the dog. They drive back to&nbsp;
a warehouse and start counting the money. 
&nbsp;

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:09.200
Outside, a policeman arrives looking for the&nbsp;
robbers. He holds them at gunpoint but Bandit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:15.200
saves his masters by attacking the policeman.&nbsp;
Manny and Willy manage to escape while the dog&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:21.440
is captured. Somewhere else, a fifteen-year-old&nbsp;
boy named Owen is riding his bicycle down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:27.680
neighborhood. He is suddenly stopped by a group of&nbsp;
bullies. They push him around and call him names&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:33.040
even though Owen tries to befriend them. A girl&nbsp;
from a neighboring house feels bad for him and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:38.240
lets her dog out to chase the bullies away. Owen&nbsp;
thanks the girl and returns home to his mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:44.080
Joanne. Owen’s father died a year ago because&nbsp;
of an illness. Ever since, the family has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:48.880
facing financial problems. They have moved&nbsp;
to the town in hopes of new opportunities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.680
and to be closer to their only relative,&nbsp;
Auntie Deb. Now that they have settled in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:59.120
Owen wants to get a pet dog. Joanne is&nbsp;
skeptical, but she cannot say no to her son.
&nbsp;

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.640
In the meantime, Manny and Willy are tense because&nbsp;
they can no longer make money. Manny wants to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:11.120
Bandit back but Willy insists he train a new dog.&nbsp;
He even steals a dog but Manny refuses to train&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.240
anyone other than Bandit. He gets on his laptop&nbsp;
and searches all the dog shelters in the town.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.520
Only a few minutes in, he sees that Bandit is&nbsp;
being held in the Heart Rescue dog Adoption&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:26.960
center. Owen and his mother get to the shelter&nbsp;
before them. Auntie Deb thinks bringing a dog home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:32.800
is a bad idea but Joanne insists on fulfilling her&nbsp;
son’s wishes. The owner of the adoption center,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:38.480
Trevor, is a friendly man who seems to be&nbsp;
interested in Joanne. He introduces Owen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:44.080
to Bandit and the two instantly get alone. A&nbsp;
while later, the family brings Bandit home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.480
After they leave, Manny arrives at the&nbsp;
shelter and asks to meet Bandit. 
&nbsp;

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.800
When he discovers that he has already been&nbsp;
adopted, he goes through the adoption forms and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:58.800
finds out Owen’s address. He plans to get his dog&nbsp;
back one way or the other. At Owen’s house, Joanne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.840
and Deb discuss the family’s financial issues. Deb&nbsp;
wants Joanne to borrow money from her but Joanne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:09.120
wants to do everything on her own. Bandit hears&nbsp;
the word “money” and is instantly alerted. Yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.080
he refuses to come out from under the bed.&nbsp;
Owen tries to bribe him with toys and treats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.200
but the dog still doesn’t move. He thinks that&nbsp;
Bandit doesn’t like him but his mother asks him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.760
to have some patience. After the family goes&nbsp;
to sleep, Bandit finally comes out from under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:29.200
the bed and runs outside. At the same time,&nbsp;
Manny and Willy arrive there looking for him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.720
Manny sneaks inside the house through the pet door&nbsp;
while Bandit runs away to a nearby restaurant. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:40.000
guests think he is cute and let him play around.&nbsp;
But when they are busy, Bandit steals money from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:45.840
a woman’s purse and returns home. On his way,&nbsp;
he also steals from a homeless person. Back at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.720
the house the robbers drive away after looking&nbsp;
for Bandit everywhere but not finding him. 
&nbsp;

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:56.000
The following day, Owen takes the dog to a vet to&nbsp;
make sure he doesn’t have any illness. The doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.880
checks him and confirms that Bandit is healthier&nbsp;
than ever. Everything goes well until after they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:06.400
leave and the doctor notices his wallet is&nbsp;
missing. That afternoon, Owen is playing with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.520
toys in the backyard when the girl who saved him&nbsp;
from the bullies approaches him. She introduces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:17.440
herself as Lily and asks to be his friend. The&nbsp;
two chat for a while before she leaves. Later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:22.240
Owen and Bandit are returning from the grocery&nbsp;
store when the bullies stop them again. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:27.680
make fun of Owen and snatch his bag of groceries.&nbsp;
Bandit sees a twenty-dollar bill inside their bag&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:32.400
and steals it without anyone noticing. When&nbsp;
the bullies threaten to throw stones at them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:38.560
Owen takes a stand for himself and hits them with&nbsp;
tomatoes. Back at home, Joanne is crying because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:44.320
she had a miscommunication at her work and got&nbsp;
fired on her first day. Auntie Deb and her husband&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:49.520
try to console her when Owen arrives at the house.&nbsp;
Although Joanne pretends like everything is going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:54.560
great in front of him, Owen understands that&nbsp;
his mother is having financial difficulties. 
&nbsp;

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.880
Suddenly, Bandit hands him the twenty dollar&nbsp;
bill he had stolen from the bullies. Before he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:03.760
can figure out where the money came from, someone&nbsp;
rings their doorbell. It is one of the bullies and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:08.880
his mother complaining about someone stealing his&nbsp;
lunch money. They also accuse Owen of hitting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:14.880
kids. The woman threatens to call animal control&nbsp;
and leaves. Owen realizes that his dog was the one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:20.240
who stole the money. The following day, they go to&nbsp;
the park to train. Owen firmly believes that what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:25.840
Bandit did was wrong and wants him to learn to&nbsp;
choose dog treats instead of money. While he is at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:31.600
it, Lily comes to talk to him, along with her dog&nbsp;
Lucy. The two decide to go on a date to see the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.960
Christmas decorations around town. After spending&nbsp;
the entire day together and having a lot of fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:42.320
they hug and return home. The following day,&nbsp;
Joanne goes to the dog shelter to meet Trevor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:46.480
She initially wants to talk about Bandit’s&nbsp;
relationship with her son but the direction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:54.000
of the conversation changes when Trevor mentions&nbsp;
he wants to date her. Joanne is unsure because she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:59.680
has never been with anyone other than her husband&nbsp;
but she agrees to go out on a date anyway. 
&nbsp;

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:05.200
Somewhere else, Owen is training Bandit in a park.&nbsp;
Bandit notices a van and follows it to the bank.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:09.600
Two policemen are loading the van with money&nbsp;
from the state’s treasury. The dog hides under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:14.320
the vehicle and steals a bag of money when&nbsp;
no one is looking. While he is running away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:20.240
one of the policemen named Albert sees him but&nbsp;
doesn’t think much of it. Soon, they realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:25.520
a bag is missing and start searching for it.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, Owen finds Bandit under a bush with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:29.600
bundles of money. Although the kid knows&nbsp;
that talking the money would be a crime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:35.040
he does so anyway to help his mother. On his way&nbsp;
back home, he meets auntie Deb who hands him an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:40.400
envelope with a check for a thousand dollars.&nbsp;
She asks him to hand it to Joanne as an early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:45.600
Christmas present from her side. Back in the&nbsp;
bank, detective Decker is assigned to find out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:50.720
where the money went. Albert claims that it might&nbsp;
have been stolen by a dog. While everyone laughs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.840
the detective believes him since he also worked&nbsp;
on the last robbery that Bandit was a part of.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:01.280
On reaching home, Owen tears the check and keeps&nbsp;
a couple thousand dollars in the envelope instead.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:05.520
Joanne thinks that her sister is trying to&nbsp;
help her like always and keeps the money. 
&nbsp;

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:09.680
The following day, Owen decides to return&nbsp;
the money without being caught. But after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:14.400
seeing the news about the stolen money on&nbsp;
TV, he gets scared and changes his mind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.640
When his mother asks him what is wrong, he&nbsp;
makes an excuse saying that he has to go out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:26.160
on a date with Lily. After the interaction,&nbsp;
he goes to Lily’s house and asks her out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:31.040
Somewhere else, the robbers also see the news&nbsp;
and figure out that Bandit has stolen the money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:35.600
They decide to get it from Owen before he is&nbsp;
caught. That way, the blame will fall on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:41.600
kid and they will have the money. Owen and Lily&nbsp;
go to a candy store where he buys her a lollipop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:46.720
The other kids surround him, asking him to buy one&nbsp;
for them as well. To impress Lily, he agrees to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:51.520
buy them everything they want. The girls who used&nbsp;
to ignore him before, start to flirt with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:56.800
much to Lily’s annoyance. He brings the entire&nbsp;
group to a toy shop and buys them everything they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:02.720
pick. Lily asks him if he can afford it to which&nbsp;
he smugly replies that it is his money. Lily is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:08.640
unsettled by his new personality but doesn’t say&nbsp;
anything. Outside the toy store, a couple stops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:13.840
to play with Bandit but he steals the woman’s&nbsp;
necklace and runs away. At the same time, Albert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.800
recognises him and starts chasing the dog.
Eventually, the couple and all the kids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:24.320
follow behind. Bandit manages to fool them and&nbsp;
gets away after hiding inside a photo booth. Back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:30.400
home, Joanne and Trevor return from a date and are&nbsp;
about to kiss but are interrupted by Bandit. Soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:35.120
the truth comes out and the family is brought&nbsp;
to the police station along with the dog.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:39.920
A policeman interrogates them and asks them if&nbsp;
they have the money. While the others deny it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:45.440
Owen realizes his mistake and hands the bag of&nbsp;
money to the officer. He decides to let the family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:51.360
go since they had no part in the robbery. However,&nbsp;
he has to hand Bandit to animal control where he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:57.520
will soon be put down. Owen and Bandit share an&nbsp;
emotional goodbye before separating. He returns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:02.720
home sad that his best friend is about to be&nbsp;
killed. Trevor tries to cheer him up claiming that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:08.640
he can choose any dog from the shelter. However,&nbsp;
Owen knows that no one can replace Bandit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:14.560
At night, Joanne comes to his room to check on&nbsp;
him and finds him asleep. But, Owen had only been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:20.640
pretending. He has decided to go to animal control&nbsp;
headquarters to release his dog. He packs up his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:25.760
bags with clothes and other necessities, planning&nbsp;
to move to a different state with Bandit. 
&nbsp;

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:30.800
As Owen is about to leave, Lily stops him outside&nbsp;
the house. Owen thinks that she is about to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:37.200
everyone but in contrast, she wishes him luck and&nbsp;
kisses him on the cheek. Following that, he cycles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:42.320
to the headquarters and swiftly releases Bandit&nbsp;
from his cage. But, what he doesn’t know is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:48.400
Manny and Willy are waiting for him outside, ready&nbsp;
to kidnap the dog. When Owen tries to scream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:52.960
they abduct him and bring him to a warehouse.&nbsp;
They had hoped to get the money that Bandit had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:58.400
stolen from the bank and are disappointed after&nbsp;
finding out that Owen returned it. So instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:04.080
Manny leaves Willy to look after Owen and goes to&nbsp;
rob a bank with Bandit. The next morning, Joanne&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:10.160
goes into Owen’s room to wake him up, only to find&nbsp;
him missing. In the meantime, Manny poses as blind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:16.000
and enters a bank with Bandit. He uses a guard’s&nbsp;
gun to threaten the cashier and asks for money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:21.040
Bandit and the cashier go to the vault to fill&nbsp;
up the bag. When the dog returns with the money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:26.640
he and Manny drive away. Back in the warehouse,&nbsp;
Owen gets his hands on a gun and threatens Willy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:32.000
to go to the police. Just then, Manny and&nbsp;
the dog arrive at the place. On seeing Willy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:38.000
trying to attack Owen, Bandit jumps on him. They&nbsp;
struggle and the dog is shot in the process.
&nbsp;

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:42.960
The policemen come to the warehouse at the&nbsp;
right time and get the dog to a vet. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:48.000
Manny and Willy drive away while being pursued by&nbsp;
a police car. They are happy that they at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:53.440
have the money but soon realize that Bandit fooled&nbsp;
them. Instead of the money, the bag is filled with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:58.880
sticky notes. In the following scene, Owen is in&nbsp;
the hospital praying that the dog is alive. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:04.160
doctor comes outside the operating room and gives&nbsp;
him the good news. A few days later, the town’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:09.760
mayor honors Bandit and Owen for their bravery and&nbsp;
helping the police to capture the robbers. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:15.600
are given ten thousand dollars prize money each.&nbsp;
The entire town praises them for their bravery. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:21.440
the last scene, we see that Bandit and Lily's dog&nbsp;
have made several puppies together. Owen and Lily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:34.160
sell the puppies to people in a yard sale. 
